---
mm: 1.0
kind: test
name: build
use: mm.test
use: mm.build
use: mm.configure
unit: tests/mm/build/config.cpp
unit: tests/mm/build/manifest.cpp
unit: tests/mm/build/platform.cpp
unit: tests/mm/build/compile.cpp
unit: tests/mm/build/graph.cpp
unit: tests/mm/build/external.cpp
unit: tests/mm/build/graft.cpp
unit: tests/main.cpp
---

# mm.build test target

`use: mm.build` pulls in mm.mdy transitively, so this manifest never names the parser's units or their ordering.

Units mirror the module's exported partitions — one suite per partition
(`:config`, `:manifest`, `:platform`, `:compile`, `:graph`, `:external`) —
listed in the same order as the partition interfaces declare them.
`graft.cpp` is the cross-partition integration suite: grafting a foreign
root through `LoadPolicy.external` touches the walk, the artifact context
and library wiring by definition. The internal `:detail` partition is
deliberately untested here; its helpers are exercised through the
partition suites and are not part of the exported API.
